From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:25:56 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77779: Take the charging status from the
 charger

The gauge can't tell charging from discharging by itself, so the driver
reported STATUS as unknown, and desktops showed no charging state. When
a charger supplies the gauge (power-supplies, or supplied_to from the
charger driver), report that charger's status instead.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77779_battery.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77779_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77779_battery.c
index d5a9dfe2a..dbefc3c23 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77779_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77779_battery.c
@@ -118,8 +118,13 @@ static int max77779_get_property(struct power_supply *supply,
 		value->intval = ((s16)reg * 10) / 256;
 		return 0;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
-		/* The charger and external-power detection are separate devices. */
-		value->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
+		/*
+		 * The charger is a separate device: take its status when one
+		 * supplies this gauge, else report it as unknown.
+		 */
+		if (power_supply_get_property_from_supplier(supply, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS,
+							    value))
+			value->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
 		return 0;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY:
 		value->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_TECHNOLOGY_LION;
